        rdfs:comment                   "Handkerchief 'Derby Winner' of printed silk, made by Welch, Margetson & Co. Ltd, England, 1867"@en , "Handkerchief of printed silk 'Derby Winner'. In the centre is a jockey with a purple cap and shirt mounted on the Derby winner for 1867 with an inscription. Around this, in fancy scrollwork cartouches with clover leaves are the printed names of the Derby winners since 1780. The outer edge is blue."@en ;
